  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/67c2114d-b072-4f46-8a6d-afa2ed7ed994-image.png\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 205px;\" /><br /><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is the position of the face of man then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> is the position of the image of a face. As&nbsp;the image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the object.<math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> From concave mirror image is 15cm behind the mirror. So, <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>. So, the radius of curvature,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>",
